## §2 — PLAN

### 2.1 Parameter table (every variable → CONFIG key; specimen value = default)
Top-level: `stageW 640 · stageH 440 · cols 7 · rows 5 · firstDay 1 · panelW 250 · panelH 185 · panelY 55 · panelR 10 · calShiftPx 95 · tasksGapPx 20 · numeralFontPx 15 · titleFontPx 13 · labelFontPx 13 · fontFamily "Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif" · daysTitle "DAYS" · tasksTitle "TASKS" · timelineLabelA "SUCH-AND-SUCH DATE" · timelineLabelB "THIS TIME" · ringEarlyIdx 15 · ringLateIdx 33 · ringRPx 13 · strikeStrokePx 2 · labelStrikeStrokePx 2 · dropDash "5 5" · timelineY 372 · timelineTicks 15 · figureCx 400 · figureScale 1 · tasksRowsJoin 3 · tasksRowsTotal 5 · strikes1Target 20 · strikes2Target 26 · strikes3Target 32 · strikesFinalTarget 35 · gridDurMs 1200 · strikes1DurMs 2000 · dropDurMs 600 · labelsDurMs 600 · hold1DurMs 1000 · tasksDurMs 1000 · sweep3DurMs 2000 · finalDurMs 2000 · holdMs 2000 · easeGrid/easeStrikes/easeDrop/easeLabels/easeTasks/easeFinal "linear" · palette {bg #000000, ink #f4f4f4, faint #7d7d7d, panel #f4f4f4, strike #f4f4f4}`.
Derived (named, never stored): dayCount = cols×rows (=35; count assertion: source-count 35 = built-count 35, harness-printed) · day label of cell i = String(firstDay + i) · cellW = panelW/cols · cellH = panelH/rows · strike order = index order 0..dayCount−1 (RTL reading is a rendering direction; the sweep's index order is the priced allocation of the census's row-wise progression) · phase starts: gridStart=0 · strikes1Start=gridStart+gridDurMs (=1200) · dropStart=strikes1Start+strikes1DurMs (=3200) · labelsStart=dropStart+dropDurMs (=3800) · hold1End=labelsStart+labelsDurMs (=4400) · tasksStart=hold1End+hold1DurMs (=5400) · sweep3Start=tasksStart+tasksDurMs (=6400) · finalStart=sweep3Start+sweep3DurMs (=8400) · completeAtMs=finalStart+finalDurMs (=10400) · durationMs=completeAtMs+holdMs (=12400) · strikeFloat(t): 0 before strikes1Start; →strikes1Target across strikes1; →strikes2Target across tasks phase; →strikes3Target across sweep3; →strikesFinalTarget across final · cell i strikeP = clamp(strikeFloat − i, 0, 1) (ring cells' strikeP drives their ⊗ cross instead of a slash — a ring cell renders slash XOR cross, never both) · ringEarly: plain ring forms across the last 25% of grid phase; its CROSS draws with its cell's strikeP across strikes1 (plain → ⊗ conversion) · ringLate: plain ring forms across the last 20% of strikes1; converts to ⊗ across the final phase (crossP = finalP) · drop1P = gridP (census: drop-line 1 is set at first calendar frame; it falls from ringEarly's cell) · drop2P across drop phase (falls from ringLate's cell) · labelA strikeP + labelB opacity across labels phase · labelB strikeP across final phase (both label strikes X-form per §1.4 (3), drawn from each label's strikeP) · arcOpacity = gridP × (1 − finalP) · tasksP across tasks phase (panel slides from x+tasksTravelPx with opacity; tasksTravelPx = panelW×0.4 derived) · tasksRowsVisible = tasksRowsJoin during tasks phase, → tasksRowsTotal across sweep3 · calShiftP = tasksP (calendar group translates −calShiftPx × tasksP). **Validation:** durations >0 finite; targets strictly increasing and ≤ dayCount (final target = dayCount: every cell marked in the final state, per the cured §1.1 (3)); ring indices distinct and < dayCount; tasksRowsJoin ≤ tasksRowsTotal; a violating CONFIG is rejected by validateConfig, never rendered.

### 2.2 Construction choice
**DOM/SVG single-stage scene (chosen):** one SVG; background rect; calendar group (panel rect + title tab + per-cell numeral text + per-cell strike line + ring marks) translating with calShiftP; tasks group (panel + title + checkbox rows) joining at tasks phase; timeline group (line + ticks + two labels with strike crosses + figure + dashed arc); dashed drop-lines from ring cells to the timeline. All geometry from `stateAt(cfg,t)`, a pure function evaluable in node; `window.__T243` exposed.
Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element ink measurement the A6 fit leg needs. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function (A11 receipts impossible). Photographic/generated imagery — approaches the specimen; the technique is the draw-on order, carried by geometry.
**Named deferrals (lawful, priced):** (1) Window head (source 13–17 s, T242's bars) — outside this technique; the allocation discards it (departure table §2.3). (2) The figure's chest-star crack at 26 s — the next beat's glyph; the build holds the final state. (3) The tail transition (≥26.5 s: dimming panels, tiny population figures) — next scene, not built. (4) The "perhaps…" annotation at 23 s — caption-adjacent scene text, not technique; not built. (5) Persian numeral glyphs + Persian label texts — the build renders CONFIG Latin strings (numerals derived from firstDay, labels as CONFIG text); the technique is the order + marks, not the specimen's language — the swap test re-labels freely, which is the parameterization proof. (6) The source's calendar entrance is unobserved (inside the 15→17 s gap): the build's grid phase is an ALLOCATION expanding that entrance so the named order reads — priced in §2.5, departure-tabled in §2.3.

### 2.3 Census-anchor mapping (A10.2) + A11 assertions
Window-start offset: **t=0 allocation** — build 0 ms = source 17.0 s (segment-relative 4000 ms); build instant = census seg-rel − 4000 for the lifecycle anchors, with the opening-expansion departure below.
**Departure table:** (a) census CP0/CP2000 (seg-rel 0/2000, T242 bars) have NO build counterpart (deferral 1). (b) Census CP4000 (seg-rel 4000) shows the panel ASSEMBLED with 7 strikes already — the build expands the entrance: its grid phase (0–1200) draws panel+numerals with 0 strikes, so the build reaches "grid complete" at 1200 where the census has it at seg-rel 4000; every later anchor is then offset by the build's own phase durations, and the mapping below binds build states to census STATES (not to raw seg-rel arithmetic). (c) Census CP14000 (seg-rel 14000, transition out) has no build counterpart (deferral 3); the build's final hold stands in its place.
**State mapping (build instant → census state it must equal):** build 4400 (labels end) ≡ CP6000 state (strikes 20 · ringCross ⊗ · ringLate plain · drops 2 · labelA struck · labelB present unstruck · tasks absent) · build 5400 (hold1 end) ≡ CP7000 state (identical — the hold) · build 6400 (tasks end) ≡ CP8000 state (tasks 3 rows · strikes 26 · calendar shifted) · build 8400 (sweep3 end) ≡ CP10000 state (tasks 5 rows · strikes 32) · build 10400 (final end) ≡ CP12000 state (strikes 35 — all cells marked · ringLate ⊗ · labelB struck · arc 0) · build 11400 (hold mid) ≡ CP12000 state (full-state equality, crack deferred).
Assertions (CONFIG expression → evaluated instant; raw phase values printed; full predicates over ALL cells):
- P0 grid start: `stateAt(CONFIG, 0)` → gridP 0, strikesFull 0, tasksP 0.
- P1 grid complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.gridDurMs)` → 1200 ms: gridP 1, numerals 35/35, strikeFloat 0, ringEarly opacity 1.
- P2 strikes1 mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, strikes1Start + CONFIG.strikes1DurMs/2)` → 2200 ms: strikeFloat 10, strikesFull 10.
- P3 strikes1 complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, strikes1Start + CONFIG.strikes1DurMs)` → 3200 ms: strikeFloat 20, strikesFull 20, ringEarly crossP 1 (plain → ⊗ conversion complete; its cell's strikeP(15) = 1 rendered as the cross, no slash on that cell), ringLate plain 1 (crossP 0).
- P4 drop-line 2 complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, dropStart + CONFIG.dropDurMs)` → 3800 ms: drop2P 1, drop1P 1.
- P5 labels complete (= CP6000 state): `stateAt(CONFIG, labelsStart + CONFIG.labelsDurMs)` → 4400 ms: labelAStrikeP 1, labelB opacity 1, labelBStrikeP 0, tasksP 0.
- P6 hold identity: `stateAt(CONFIG, hold1End + CONFIG.hold1DurMs/2)` fully equal to P5 state (full-state JSON equality, t excluded).
- P7 tasks joined (= CP8000 state): `stateAt(CONFIG, tasksStart + CONFIG.tasksDurMs)` → 6400 ms: tasksP 1, tasksRowsVisible 3, strikeFloat 26, calShift = calShiftPx.
- P8 sweep3 complete (= CP10000 state): `stateAt(CONFIG, sweep3Start + CONFIG.sweep3DurMs)` → 8400 ms: strikeFloat 32, tasksRowsVisible 5.
- P9 final complete (= CP12000 state): `stateAt(CONFIG, finalStart + CONFIG.finalDurMs)` → 10400 ms: strikeFloat 35, strikesFull 35 (every cell marked: slashes + the two ring cells' crosses), cell 34 (day 35) strikeP 1 — its slash lands in the final phase, ringLate crossP 1, labelBStrikeP 1, arcOpacity 0.
- P10 hold identity: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs + 500)` fully equal to P9 state. durationMs = 12400.
- **Fixed census probes (C*) with EXECUTABLE CONFIG-derived companions (sibling-cure form):** each C probe's instant is a literal census-mapped build instant (4400/5400/6400/8400/10400); its companion evaluates the SAME predicate at the CONFIG-derived phase-end expression (e.g. C@4400's companion = `stateAt(CONFIG, labelsStart + CONFIG.labelsDurMs)`), both evaluated instants printed, and under the timing swap (strikes1DurMs 2000→3000) the companion instant MOVES 4400→5400 while the fixed probe's evaluated strikeFloat changes 20→(4400−1200−1000)/3000×20… (printed exactly by the harness) — the paired receipt form.
- **Zero-state anchors (guards cmd 8):** at P1, strikeFloat = 0 evaluated from the CONFIG expression (strikes1Start − gridDurMs = 0 progress) — printed as expression + observed per-cell strike sum = 0; at P0, tasksP = 0 and drop2P = 0 likewise expression-bound.

### 2.4 Verification plan (instruments named)
- Execute checklist: (1) cut segment.mp4 from source.mp4 at 12.5–27.5 s (window ±0.5 handles), libx264/yuv420p + AAC faststart, ffprobe filed; (2) build recreation.html (CONFIG at top, pure stateAt, window.__T243 exposed); (3) build comparison.html — labels verbatim: "ORIGINAL — ensan.besham Hope = Failure (?) @ 13–27 s" · "RECREATION — T243 Calendar-of-days panel, parameterized" · sync: ONE shared start timestamp drives both sides; the video (15.0 s cut) maps to build clamp((videoT−2.0)×(12400/13000), 0, durationMs) — cut starts 12.5, build zero at source 17.0 = cut-relative 4.5 s; the mapping compresses the cut's 13–17 s head + 26–27.5 s tail into the build's opening/closing 2.0 s shoulders so both sides reach the final state together (named comparison allocation; the check tests head (wall 0 → build 0), anchor (wall 6.5 s = source 19 ≡ build 4400 state region), and tail (wall ≥15 s → build durationMs hold state) · durationMs DERIVED at runtime from recreation.html's CONFIG · phone stacking @media ≤560px; (4) own checks §5 legs 1–3 + A6 legs.
- Swap test: content — firstDay 1→10 (labels 10..44 regenerate), daysTitle→"WEEKS", timelineLabelA→"AFTER THE DEADLINE", timelineLabelB→"NEXT TIME"; grid — cols 7→6 AND rows 5→4 in a scratch CONFIG (dayCount 35→24, targets set explicitly in the swap config: strikes targets 14/18/22/24, ring indices early 9 / late 20 — the technique must still read); timing — `strikes1DurMs 2000→3000`, PAIRED receipt: (a) fixed probe C@4400's evaluated strikeFloat changes (printed both values), AND (b) the companion instant for the labels-complete event moves 4400→5400 with its CONFIG expression printed at both values; palette — `palette.strike #f4f4f4→#e8b13a` (observed strike stroke in render output).
- Purity: guards cmd1 grep `segment\.mp4|source\.mp4|<video|<img|DFFiiPMMAC3` on recreation.html → specimen hits 0 (`url(#id)` in-file refs classified, not counted); asset inventory = recreation.html alone.
- A6 legs: fit-table.md (PIL rendered measurement, stand-in font DejaVu Sans named — measured ink for day numerals (1- and 2-digit rows), panel titles, timeline labels incl. swapped long label, at the 360 px stage) + config-census.md (all literals classified; every CONFIG key incl. `palette.*` resolved to value-flowing sites; CSS-variable check — none used).
- jev-prewave after legs 1–3 + A6, payload per its contract (A6 outputs verbatim per A10.1 + this mapping §2.3); five-lens Codex wave (motion · timing · purity · reusability · readability) only on FIRE-WAVE; bar avg ≥85, min ≥70.

### 2.5 Failure points (priced)
- Opening-expansion timing risk: the source's entrance is unobserved; a timing lens pricing the build's 1200 ms grid phase against a cut-in source may dock it — answered by the §2.3 departure table filed before the wave; the alternative (opening on the assembled panel) would delete the technique's first named phase (grid draw-on) entirely.
- Strike-order direction: census rows strike top-first; within-row direction is below census resolution (strikes appear between 2 s frames as row blocks). The build's index-order sweep is the priced allocation; a motion lens may price RTL-vs-LTR — the WHY in scores.md names it if the minimum lands there.
- Ring lifecycle complexity: three ring beats (early plain → overstruck · cross ⊗ · late plain → ⊗) is the item's densest machinery; a readability lens may price the small rings (ringRPx 13 at 360 px stage ≈ 7 px radius) as weak — accepted risk, ring radius is CONFIG and the fit leg measures numeral ink, not rings (named scope).
- Label fitting: "SUCH-AND-SUCH DATE" (18 chars) + the swap's "AFTER THE DEADLINE" at labelFontPx 13 must fit the 640 stage and the 360 px stage — measured in the fit leg incl. swapped labels; a HIT is cured by CONFIG font size, never code shrink.
- Tasks-panel shift: the calendar's −95 px shift at tasks-join must not push numerals off-panel (panel translates whole — numerals ride inside; asserted via calShift receipt at P7).
- Render-proof limitation: no browser binary in this seat — PIXEL-UNVERIFIED carried to scores.md; comparison page is the render surface.
- Plateau (A2): FIRST ATTEMPT — no prior average. **Predicted minimum lens: timing/tempo** — hypothesis: the opening expansion + state-mapped (not time-mapped) anchors are the honest weak point; if the wave's minimum is another lens, the WHY in scores.md names it.

